    <description>ALF-RS-08 (LFRDN-338) FR1: Quick Action screen flow on Quote that creates a Vehicle Reservation with the minimum the Sales Rep must decide (contract type, vehicle source, deposit), then derives everything else from the Quote and its Opportunity - Account, Contact, Opportunity, Quote link, Start Date, and Vehicle Price Total. Replaces the plain related-list &quot;New&quot; button, which carried no context and required the rep to re-enter the account/opportunity/vehicle by hand (the exact gap that tripped AF_VR_VehicleRequired on a blank form). Blocks entirely while the Quote&apos;s own discount is still Pending approval, matching the HLD&apos;s step 2 -&gt; step 3 sequencing (&quot;the quotation document is generated after approval&quot; comes before &quot;Reserve&quot;). All downstream governance - expiry date, approval routing against the deposit threshold matrix, pricing sync - is left to the existing before-save flows on AF_VehicleReservation__c; this flow only creates the record and hands off.

The Available Vehicles table is restricted to Vehicle records with the Regular_Vehicle record type (looked up by DeveloperName rather than a hardcoded Id, so this survives a promotion to QA/UAT where the RecordTypeId differs) - Demo_Vehicle records exist purely for demoing the catalog/media experience and were never meant to be reservable stock.

CHANGED 2026-09-19: added a same-vehicle shortcut. The rep is asked up front whether to reserve the vehicle already associated with this Quote or pick a different one. Vehicle source (Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleId) prefers the Quote&apos;s own QuoteLineItem.AF_Vehicle__c (the real vehicle line on this specific Quote, via Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line) and falls back to Opportunity.AF_SelectedVehicle__c only if the Quote has no vehicle line item - CORRECTED same day: the first version of this change wrongly sourced only from the Opportunity mirror field, not the Quote itself, which is what &quot;the vehicle associated with this quote&quot; actually means. Answering Yes (default) skips both vehicle-picker screens entirely. Answering No, or neither source having a vehicle, falls through to the existing Decide_Source_Type picker path unchanged. The Available Vehicles table&apos;s own AF_ReservationStatus__c=&apos;Available&apos; filter (kept as-is) already excludes any vehicle held by a live reservation (Requested/Pending Approval/Reserved) via AF_VehicleReservationStatusSync - confirmed still live against real DEV data, not rebuilt.

FIXED 2026-09-20: the same-vehicle shortcut was silently creating reservations with a blank AF_Vehicle__c and failing AF_VR_VehicleSourceMatchesVehicle on every attempt, in both DEV and QA - confirmed via debug log (AF_Vehicle__c=null on the actual insert, despite Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line/Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleId correctly resolving the vehicle for the confirmation screen text and passing Decide_Same_Vehicle&apos;s own IS NOT NULL guard). Root cause: Formula_EffectiveVehicleId referenced the live record-lookup formula chain again at Create_Reservation time instead of the value already confirmed at the decision, and that re-evaluation returned blank. Fix: Assign_SameVehicleId now captures Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleId into a stored Var_SameVehicleId variable immediately after Decide_Same_Vehicle confirms it&apos;s populated, and Formula_EffectiveVehicleId reads from that stored variable instead of re-deriving it - removes any dependency on formula re-evaluation timing at the actual DML step.

FIXED 2026-09-23 (LFRDN-694): Decide_Source_Type previously merged &quot;In Stock&quot; and &quot;In Transit / Ordered&quot; into one OR-rule routing to a single Get_Available_Vehicles query that never filtered on AF_InventoryStatus__c at all - so both selections showed every available vehicle regardless of actual stock status. Split into two separate decision rules, each routing to its own record-type lookup and its own vehicle query: Get_Available_Vehicles now additionally requires AF_InventoryStatus__c = &apos;In Stock&apos;, and a new Get_Available_Vehicles_Transit requires it to be &apos;In Transit&apos; or &apos;Ordered&apos; (via filterLogic &quot;(1 AND 2 AND 3) AND (4 OR 5)&quot;, since a single field cannot equal two picklist values at once). Each feeds its own confirmation screen (Screen_ConfirmVehicle / Screen_ConfirmVehicle_Transit), both reusing the Table_AvailableVehicles field name so Formula_EffectiveVehicleId&apos;s existing firstSelectedRow reference needs no change regardless of which path was taken. Also added an AF_InventoryStatus__c &quot;Status&quot; column to both datatables, per the same ticket&apos;s request to show the vehicle&apos;s status directly in the picker rather than requiring the rep to trust the pre-filtered list. SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24.

REMOVED 2026-09-24 (LFRDN-720): the entire &quot;pick a different vehicle&quot; capability described above has been deleted. The rep is no longer asked Yes/No, and there is no longer any vehicle/vehicle-definition picker path. Deleted: Choice_SameVehicle_Yes/No, Choice_Source_InStock/InTransit/PreOrder, Decide_Source_Type, Screen_ConfirmVehicle, Screen_ConfirmVehicle_Transit, Screen_ConfirmVehicleDefinition, Get_Available_Vehicles, Get_Available_Vehicles_Transit, Get_Regular_Vehicle_RecordType, Get_Regular_Vehicle_RecordType_Transit, Get_Vehicle_Definitions, and the SameVehicleField/VehicleSourceTypeField screen fields. Decide_Same_Vehicle is kept but simplified: its two rules now test only whether Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleId / Formula_OpportunityVehicleDefinitionId are populated (no more rep choice in the condition), and its default path (neither populated) now routes to a new blocking screen, Screen_NoVehicleAssigned (&quot;Select a vehicle on the Opportunity/Quote before creating a reservation&quot;), instead of into the deleted picker. AF_VehicleSourceType__c on Create_Reservation, which used to read the rep&apos;s VehicleSourceTypeField choice, is now derived automatically by a new Formula_EffectiveVehicleSourceType: Pre-Order (Placeholder) when only a Vehicle Definition was resolved (no physical Vehicle yet), otherwise In Stock or In Transit / Ordered read directly off the resolved Vehicle&apos;s own AF_InventoryStatus__c - this still satisfies AF_VR_VehicleSourceMatchesVehicle without asking the rep to self-report a value that used to just be a guess. Decide_Error_Type / Screen_VehicleAlreadyHeld (the post-DML double-booking race-condition error) is untouched.

LFRDN-721/726 (2026-09-24): two more gaps closed in the same pass. LFRDN-721: added Get_Existing_Payment (Opportunity&apos;s own AF_Payment__c where AF_Status__c = &apos;Paid / Verified&apos;) and wired it onto Create_Reservation&apos;s new AF_Payment__c input - a deposit paid before a reservation existed was never being linked to the reservation created afterward. LFRDN-726: added Get_Active_Appraisal (Opportunity&apos;s IsActive=true Appraisal) so TradeInAsDepositField only shows once that appraisal&apos;s Status = &apos;Completed&apos; (previously showed unconditionally, even with no trade-in on the deal at all). Split the old single DepositAmountField in two, mutually exclusive by TradeInAsDepositField: DepositAmountField (relabeled &quot;Amount to Apply from Trade-In&quot;, defaults to Get_Active_Appraisal.AF_ActiveTradeInValue__c but stays editable since the full appraisal value isn&apos;t always what the rep wants applied) shows only when Trade-In is selected; DepositAmountCashField (&quot;Deposit Amount&quot;, unchanged cash behavior) shows only when it isn&apos;t. Formula_EffectiveDepositAmount picks whichever one actually rendered for Create_Reservation&apos;s AF_DepositAmount__c input.

LFRDN-760 fix (2026-09-27): Get_Active_Appraisal&apos;s IsActive=true filter never matched anything real - a live query confirmed zero Appraisal records in this org have IsActive=true, since nothing in the org&apos;s automation ever sets that standard field. Every genuinely-approved trade-in (AF_ApprovalStatus__c=&apos;Approved&apos;) checked live had IsActive=false and a Status other than &apos;Completed&apos; - so TradeInAsDepositField could never appear for any real approved trade-in. Replaced the query filter with AF_ApprovalStatus__c=&apos;Approved&apos; (matching FR11&apos;s &quot;approved Trade-In&quot; language), sorted by CreatedDate Desc, and changed the field&apos;s visibility rule to check Get_Active_Appraisal.Id is not null rather than re-testing Status.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_EffectiveDepositAmount</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!TradeInAsDepositField}, {!DepositAmountField}, {!DepositAmountCashField})</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_EffectiveVehicleDefinitionId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!Var_SameVehicleDefinitionId}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_EffectiveVehicleId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!Var_SameVehicleId}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_EffectiveVehicleInventoryStatus</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__c})),
    TEXT({!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__r.AF_InventoryStatus__c}),
    TEXT({!Get_Opportunity.AF_SelectedVehicle__r.AF_InventoryStatus__c})
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_EffectiveVehicleSourceType</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    ISBLANK({!Var_SameVehicleId}),
    &quot;Pre-Order (Placeholder)&quot;,
    IF(
        {!Formula_EffectiveVehicleInventoryStatus} = &quot;In Stock&quot;,
        &quot;In Stock&quot;,
        &quot;In Transit / Ordered&quot;
    )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_OpportunityVehicleDefinitionId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!Get_Opportunity.AF_VehicleModel__c}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__c})),
    {!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__c},
    {!Get_Opportunity.AF_SelectedVehicle__c}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_QuoteOrOpportunityVehicleName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__c})),
    {!Get_Quote_Vehicle_Line.AF_Vehicle__r.Name},
    {!Get_Opportunity.AF_SelectedVehicle__r.Name}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
